    {
      "title": "Auto tech cos raise $1.3 bn across 97 funding rounds in 2026 so far: Tracxn",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/start-ups/auto-tech-cos-raise-1-3-bn-across-97-funding-rounds-in-2026-so-far-tracxn-126101900654_1.html",
      "description": "India's auto tech companies raised USD 1.3 billion across 97 funding rounds so far this year, according to a report from data intelligence platform Tracxn.\nThe funding rounds were led by ride-hailing firm Rapido's USD 240 million, followed by electric two-wheeler manufacturer Simple Energy's USD 180 million and River's USD 102 million.\n\"India Auto Tech companies raised USD 1.3 billion across 97 rounds in 2026 year to date (2026 YTD) against USD 2.1 billion across 195 rounds in 2025. All funding figures are US dollar equity funding and exclude debt, grant, post-IPO and ICO funding,\" the report, India Auto Tech - 2026 YTD, said.\nAutomated parking solution provider Sotefin recorded the highest IPO market capitalisation at USD 35 million, followed by Victory EV India at USD 11 million and accessories company AutoFurnish at USD 6 million.\nThere were 10 rounds of USD 34 million or more, totalling USD 900 million during the period. These accounted for around 70 per cent of the total USD 1",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-19T10:44:53"
    }
  ]
